{"role":"tool","tool_call_id":"tool_p9Nmu00snYFzlVmqTPJT02Jq","content":"1\tCreated-Local: 2026-11-01 23:0x +0700\n2\tCoding-Agent: kimi\n3\tSession: fresh (read-only architect round r2)\n4\tMode: read-only diagnosis\n5\t\n6\t# R2: the corrected fixture still grows — the runtime retention investigation\n7\t\n8\tFollow-up to your heap ruling on yang.php P4 S8. The engineer ported your protocol exactly (commit 18ef324d on branch yang-php-p4, worktree /Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-php-p4): the PHP program now runs to NORMAL completion, the one suspended h (preserved by $it->self = $it) is located in the final heap, and engine/collect runs with that cell as the extra root. The equality assertion (N=10 vs N=1000, both cell count and deep size) is unchanged.\n9\t\n10\tResult: growth persists on all four VMs, identically:\n11\t\n12\t- N=10: 151 cells on every VM\n13\t- N=1000: 5,596 cells on every VM\n14\t- deep size grows per VM (171k -> 992k walker, 23k -> 792k semantic, 131k -> 708k stack, 444k -> 1.16M register)\n15\t\n16\tAll four \"one suspended h\" root checks pass.\n17\t\n18\t## The question\n19\t\n20\tDiagnose the retention. The candidate suspects, in the order I see them:\n21\t\n22\t1. The byGenerator path creates a fresh suspended delegating generator $j per odd iteration (yield $x->current(); $x->next();). Each $j is a statement temporary released at the loop pass's cleanup. If a SUSPENDED generator's destruction path releases fewer cells than it retained, each pass leaks a constant few cells (~5.5 per iteration fits 5,445 / 990). Read the destruction/cleanup semantics (docs/design/yang.php.md:341-348, the S8 generator runtime in src/cljc/yang/php/antlr/prelude.cljc) and check whether suspended-delegator destruction releases the delegate reference, its CVs, and its frame.\n23\t2. The byFunction path calls $x->next() twice per even iteration, resuming and suspending h repeatedly — if each suspend point accumulates (a grown continuation, a stale %capture base, a retained current/key pair per resume), h itself grows with N.\n24\t3. The identical cell counts across all four VMs suggest a source-level (prelude/lowering) retention, not a VM-specific one.\n25\t\n26\tRule: which suspect (or what else) holds, what the fix is (engineer scope), and whether the checkpoint-B gate can close with this investigation open or must wait for the fix. Read-only: do not edit."}
