{"role":"tool","tool_call_id":"tool_9RQOpTY5lTd0lQSaOoZPZow1","content":"1\t# Checkpoint-B fold reconciliation findings\n2\t\n3\t## What failed\n4\t\n5\tThe focused JVM run initially failed one assertion in\n6\t`p4-registry-is-inert-test`. It expected every value in `p4/generators-v1` to\n7\tcarry `p4/banner`, but that var is the raw generator fixture definitions. The\n8\tfolded values, including recorded oracle values and hand-pinned outputs, are in\n9\t`p4/all-fixtures`; unrecorded raw definitions remain `:pending`.\n10\t\n11\t## True post-fold invariants\n12\t\n13\t- `p4/awaiting-oracle` equals exactly the IDs of enabled fixtures whose folded\n14\t  `:oracle` is `:pending`.\n15\t- For each ID in `p4/recorded`, the matching folded fixture's `:out`, `:diag`,\n16\t  and `:uncaught` equal the recorded values. A recorded fixture has the oracle\n17\t  banner because it has a recorded result.\n18\t- Generator metadata such as `:requires` is checked on the raw\n19\t  `p4/generators-v1` definitions. Oracle state is checked on the generator\n20\t  members of `p4/all-fixtures`: the banner is expected when a record exists or\n21\t  an output is pinned; otherwise the fixture remains `:pending`.\n22\t\n23\t## Change made\n24\t\n25\tUpdated the inert-registry description and replaced the incorrect assertion on\n26\traw generator definitions with a per-fixture check against the folded\n27\t`p4/all-fixtures` view. The enabled-pending equality and recorded field\n28\tcross-check remain exact. No fixture pins or protected source files were\n29\tchanged.\n30\t\n31\t## Verification\n32\t\n33\t- Class-model namespace: **8 tests, 587 assertions, 0 failures, 0 errors**.\n34\t- All `programs-p4` consumer namespaces (`class-model-test`, `generators-test`,\n35\t  `objects-test`): **14 tests, 1,076 assertions, 6 failures, 1 error**.\n36\t  - Four failures are the reachable-heap stability assertion, one per VM. Each\n37\t    measured 151 reachable cells at 10 iterations and 5,596 at 1,000\n38\t    iterations, consistent with the branch's checkpoint-B heap measurement.\n39\t  - `objects-test` has two output mismatches (`decl-byref-param-typed-coerces`\n40\t    and `decl-byref-later-rejection-releases-earlier-param`) and one runtime\n41\t    error (`data primitive refused`, `str-concat`, wrong type). Those tests and\n42\t    the heap measurement are outside this task's authorized change scope.\n43\t- `cljstyle check test/yang/php/antlr/class_model_test.cljc`: passed.\n44\t- `clojure -M:kondo --lint test/yang/php/antlr/class_model_test.cljc test/yang/php/antlr/programs_p4.cljc`:\n45\t  **0 errors, 0 warnings**."}
{"role":"tool","tool_call_id":"tool_JWCU6SgXSqKQnmEWJi1KHtAv","content":"1\t# PHP reachable-heap fixture correction findings\n2\t\n3\t## Fixture correction\n4\t\n5\t`live-after-collection` now mirrors the Python measurement protocol. It runs\n6\tthe PHP unit through normal completion with no injected blocker, locates the\n7\tsuspended generator `h` in the final heap, asserts that exactly one matching\n8\tcell exists, and calls `engine/collect` with that cell reference as an extra\n9\troot. The source keeps `$it->self = $it`, preserving the suspended generator\n10\tthrough its deliberate cycle after module cleanup.\n11\t\n12\tThe N=10/N=1000 equality assertion is unchanged. The generator runtime and\n13\tcleanup code were not modified.\n14\t\n15\t## Result\n16\t\n17\tThe corrected fixture still grows on every VM. These are final-heap results\n18\tafter normal completion and collection rooted at the suspended `h`:\n19\t\n20\t| VM | N=10 cells / deep size | N=1000 cells / deep size |\n21\t|---|---:|---:|\n22\t| AST walker | 151 / 171,275 | 5,596 / 992,480 |\n23\t| Semantic | 151 / 23,253 | 5,596 / 792,483 |\n24\t| Stack | 151 / 131,268 | 5,596 / 708,933 |\n25\t| Register | 151 / 444,280 | 5,596 / 1,160,545 |\n26\t\n27\tThis corrected result warrants a runtime retention investigation. It does not\n28\tjustify changing the fixture or weakening its equality assertion.\n29\t\n30\t## Verification\n31\t\n32\t- Explicit slow test: `clojure -M:test -i :slow -n yang.php.antlr.generators-test`\n33\t  — **1 test, 12 assertions, 4 failures, 0 errors**. The four failures are the\n34\t  expected N=10/N=1000 equality mismatches above; all four one-suspended-`h`\n35\t  root assertions passed.\n36\t- `cljstyle check test/yang/php/antlr/generators_test.clj`: passed.\n37\t- `clojure -M:kondo --lint test/yang/php/antlr/generators_test.clj`:\n38\t  **0 errors, 0 warnings**.\n39\t- `git diff --check`: clean."}
{"role":"tool","tool_call_id":"tool_UtPDOKkbNwlygGM4PHgWrPGF","content":"120\t     (fn [x]\n121\t       (if (= x :php/null)\n122\t         :null\n123\t         (if (= x true)\n124\t           :bool\n125\t           (if (= x false)\n126\t             :bool\n127\t             (if (nil? (get x :php/type))\n128\t               (if (php/string? x)\n129\t                 :string\n130\t                 (if (not (nil? (get x :php/arr)))\n131\t                   :array\n132\t                   (if (not (nil? (get x :php/obj)))\n133\t                     :obj\n134\t                     (if (not (nil? (get x :php/ref)))\n135\t                       (php/kind (php/ref-value x))\n136\t                       (if (data/content= x (data/float64 (data/float-value x)))\n137\t                         :float\n138\t                         :int)))))\n139\t               (if (= (get x :php/type) :array) :array :obj))))))]\n140\t    [php/int? (fn [x] (= (php/kind x) :int))]\n141\t    [php/float? (fn [x] (= (php/kind x) :float))]\n142\t    [php/numk? (fn [k] (if (= k :int) true (= k :float)))]\n143\t    [php/fl\n144\t     ;; the host double of an int or float\n145\t     (fn [x] (if (php/int? x) (integer/to-float x) (data/float-value x)))]\n146\t    [php/type-name\n147\t     (fn [k]\n148\t       (if (= k :string) \"string\"\n149\t           (if (= k :int) \"int\"\n150\t               (if (= k :float) \"float\"\n151\t                   (if (= k :bool) \"bool\"\n152\t                       (if (= k :null) \"null\"\n153\t                           (if (= k :array) \"array\" \"mixed\")))))))]\n154\t\n155\t    ;; ---------------------------------------------------------------- escapes\n156\t    ;; The dynamic context is one record in one cell: every capture point\n157\t    ;; saves it and every escape restores it with :base left alone. The\n158\t    ;; handler stack is a chain of frames [kind payload rest n depth].\n159\t    [php/ctx\n160\t     (fn [handlers depth base frame]\n161\t       (assoc